        "answerType": "string",
        "hintAnswer": ["2x-4"],
        "dependencies": ["calc-diff-010b-h2"],
        "title": "Take the Limit as h approaches 0",
        "text": "Now take the limit:\n\n$f'(x) = \\lim_{h \\to 0}(2x + h - 4)$\n\nAs $h \\to 0$:\n\n$f'(x) = 2x + 0 - 4 = 2x - 4$\n\nVerification using the power rule: $\\frac{d}{dx}(x^2 - 4x + 3) = 2x - 4$ (correct!)",
